**Rate Limiting**

To implement rate limiting, you can use a simple counter to track the number of requests made within a certain time window. Here's an example:
```php
$rate_limit_window = 60; // 1 minute
$rate_limit_max_requests = 10;

$last_request_time = $_SESSION['last_request_time']?? 0;
$current_request_time = time();

if ($current_request_time - $last_request_time > $rate_limit_window) {
    $last_request_time = $current_request_time;
    $request_count = 0;
} else {
    $request_count = $_SESSION['request_count']?? 0;
    $request_count++;
    if ($request_count >= $rate_limit_max_requests) {
        header('HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests');
        exit;
    }
}

$_SESSION['last_request_time'] = $current_request_time;
$_SESSION['request_count'] = $request_count;
```
